# ==============================================================================
# GMC Thiruvallur Student Council Portal - Cloudflare Pages Environment Variables
# 100% Free Tier Compatible (Cloudflare Pages Unlimited Free Bandwidth & 500 Builds/mo)
# ==============================================================================
# In Cloudflare Pages Dashboard:
# Go to: Workers & Pages > [your-pages-project] > Settings > Environment Variables
# Paste the variables below and hit 'Save and Deploy'.
# ==============================================================================

# Note: Authentication passcodes are verified strictly server-side by the Cloudflare
# Worker. No admin secret tokens should ever be stored in VITE_ variables to prevent client bundling.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. CLOUDFLARE WORKER BACKEND URL (Optional / Decoupled)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Point this to your deployed Cloudflare Worker API.
# If left empty, the portal runs standalone with offline-ready local emulation!
# Example: https://gmc-thiruvallur-backend.your-subdomain.workers.dev
VITE_API_BASE_URL=""

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. FIREBASE CONFIGURATION (Optional - for Cloud Firestore & Firebase Auth)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If left empty, all feedback, polls, chats, and announcements persist locally in the browser!
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=""
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=""
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=""
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=""
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=""
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=""

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. SERVER SECRETS & AI KEYS (Configured in Cloudflare Worker, NOT here)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All sensitive secrets (COUNCIL_AUTH_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, GROQ_API_KEY,
# and GEMINI_API_KEY) are configured exclusively in your Cloudflare Worker
# (via wrangler secret put or Cloudflare Dashboard) to prevent exposure in client bundles.
